            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to EILEEN J. O'CONNOR, the case concerns the authority of the Commissioner of Internal Revenue to assess FICA taxes on employers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "EILEEN J. O'CONNOR",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a742e6baafb3-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to EILEEN J. O'CONNOR, it involves sections 6201, which authorizes the Treasury to make tax assessments, and 3111, which imposes a tax on employers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "EILEEN J. O'CONNOR",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a742e6baafb3-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to EILEEN J. O'CONNOR, a central dispute is whether tips are considered wages under section 3121(q), which would make them subject to FICA tax."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government; Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a742e6baafb3-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a742e6baafb3-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States (petitioner) argues that the Government\u2019s formula for calculating tip income exaggerates the amount owed and that employers lack the information needed to defend the assessments."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Power",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a742e6baafb3-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Power, the respondent argues that the tax is not authorized and that the burden of proof should lie with the government."
      }
    ],
