              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the Government\u2019s formula for calculating tip income exaggerates the amount owed to the Treasury."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a742e6baafb3-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 36,
                "start": 36
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, employers lack the information needed to defend the assessments because Congress has prohibited them from obtaining such data."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a742e6baafb3-0002-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 48,
                "start": 47
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the burden of proof should rest with the government, which is in the best position to produce the records."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Power",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a742e6baafb3-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 27
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Power, the tax on tips is not authorized by Congress, so the assessment lacks legal basis."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Power",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a742e6baafb3-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 33,
                "start": 33
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Power, because the tax is unauthorized, the burden of proof and the presumption of correctness shift to the government."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Power",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a742e6baafb3f0ebff2f7aef18ef762dc0dd8d19ea6305fc50ee430b2918a57c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a742e6baafb3-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 33,
                "start": 33
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Power, the employer does not know how credit\u2011card tips are distributed, making accurate tax calculation impossible."
        }
